{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/index.html","title":"Overview and preface","text":"Open TextbooksAbstract AlgebraGroups, rings and fieldsWikibooks contributors <p>Open Textbooks</p> Abstract Algebra <p>Groups, rings and fields</p> <p>Wikibooks contributors</p> <p>Sets and functions, groups and the Sylow theorems, rings, ideals and fields, vector spaces, modules and algebras.</p> Start reading <p>37 chapters</p>"},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/index.html#contents","title":"Contents","text":"<p>Introduction</p> <ul> <li>Section 1: Sets</li> <li>Section 2: Equivalence relations and congruence classes</li> <li>Section 3: Functions</li> <li>Section 4: Binary Operations</li> <li>Section 5: Linear Algebra</li> <li>Section 6: Number Theory</li> </ul> <p>Group Theory</p> <ul> <li>Section 7: Definition of groups, very basic properties</li> <li>Section 8: Group</li> <li>Section 9: Subgroup</li> <li>Section 10: Cyclic groups</li> <li>Section 11: Permutation groups</li> <li>Section 12: Homomorphism</li> <li>Section 13: Normal subgroups and Quotient groups</li> <li>Section 14: Products and Free Groups</li> <li>Section 15: Group actions on sets</li> <li>Section 16: Composition series</li> <li>Section 17: The Sylow Theorems</li> </ul> <p>Rings</p> <ul> <li>Section 18: Rings, ideals, ring homomorphisms</li> <li>Section 19: Rings</li> <li>Section 20: Ring Homomorphisms</li> <li>Section 21: The hierarchy of rings</li> <li>Section 22: Ideals</li> <li>Section 23: Integral domains</li> <li>Section 24: Fraction Fields</li> <li>Section 25: Polynomial Rings</li> </ul> <p>Chapters</p> <ul> <li>Section 26: Fields</li> <li>Section 27: Vector Spaces</li> </ul> <p>Modules</p> <ul> <li>Section 28: Modules</li> <li>Section 29: Hypercomplex numbers</li> </ul> <p>Algebras</p> <ul> <li>Section 30: Algebras</li> <li>Section 31: Boolean algebra</li> <li>Section 32: Clifford Algebras</li> <li>Section 33: Quaternions</li> </ul> <p>Further Abstract Algebra</p> <ul> <li>Section 34: Category theory</li> <li>Section 35: Lattice theory</li> <li>Section 36: Matroids</li> </ul> <p>Chapters</p> <ul> <li>Section 37: Authors</li> </ul>"},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/index.html#about-this-book","title":"About this book","text":"<p>An undergraduate course in abstract algebra: the foundations (sets, equivalence relations, functions, the integers), group theory (subgroups, cyclic and permutation groups, homomorphisms, normal subgroups and quotients, group actions, composition series, the Sylow theorems), rings, ideals, integral domains, fraction fields and polynomial rings, fields, vector spaces and modules, algebras (Boolean and Clifford algebras, quaternions), and a glimpse of category theory, lattices and matroids.</p> <p>From Wikibooks · CC BY-SA 4.0</p><p>Abstract Algebra, a Wikibooks textbook, by its contributors. This book is not stored in this library: each chapter is read from Wikibooks when it is opened, shown in this library's format, and ends with its own attribution. Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0. Modified: converted to this format.</p>"},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/algebras.html","title":"Section 30: Algebras","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/algebras.html#301-algebras-over-a-field","title":"30.1 Algebras over a Field","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/algebras.html#302-quivers-and-path-algebras","title":"30.2 Quivers and Path Algebras","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/authors.html","title":"Section 37: Authors","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/binary-operations.html","title":"Section 4: Binary Operations","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-abstract-algebra/binary-operations.html#41-properties","title":"4.1 Properties","text